<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts" xml:lang="en-US"><voice name="en-us-emma:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully as a neutral English listening examination narrator. Use precise pronunciation and an unhurried but natural pace. After the number, leave a short pause before the next speaker. Do not separate individual words or sound robotic."><p>Number three.</p></mstts:express-as><break time="1350ms"/></voice><voice name="en-us-ava:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully for an English listening examination. Use precise pronunciation and an unhurried but natural pace. Keep the conversation responsive and human, with a brief natural pause after each turn. Do not separate individual words, sound robotic, or overemphasize information that could reveal the answer."><s>I can't meet you at the cafe this afternoon. A repair worker is coming to look at our washing machine.</s></mstts:express-as><break time="550ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-Andrew:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully for an English listening examination. Use precise pronunciation and an unhurried but natural pace. Keep the conversation responsive and human, with a brief natural pause after each turn. Do not separate individual words, sound robotic, or overemphasize information that could reveal the answer."><s>Didn't your brother say he would stay home for that?</s></mstts:express-as><break time="550ms"/></voice><voice name="en-us-ava:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully for an English listening examination. Use precise pronunciation and an unhurried but natural pace. Keep the conversation responsive and human, with a brief natural pause after each turn. Do not separate individual words, sound robotic, or overemphasize information that could reveal the answer."><s>He was supposed to, but his manager asked him to work an extra shift. The worker may arrive anytime between two and five.</s></mstts:express-as><break time="550ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-Andrew:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully for an English listening examination. Use precise pronunciation and an unhurried but natural pace. Keep the conversation responsive and human, with a brief natural pause after each turn. Do not separate individual words, sound robotic, or overemphasize information that could reveal the answer."><s>No problem. We can meet tomorrow after my class instead.</s></mstts:express-as><break time="1300ms"/></voice><voice name="en-us-emma:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully as a neutral English listening examination narrator. Say Question, pause briefly, and then read the final question with precise pronunciation. Do not emphasize any possible answer clue."><s>Question.</s></mstts:express-as><break time="350ms"/></voice><voice name="en-us-emma:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural" parameters="temperature=0.6;top_p=0.6;top_k=15;cfg_scale=1.1;enhancePronunciation=true"><mstts:express-as style="Speak slowly, clearly, and carefully as a neutral English listening examination narrator. Say Question, pause briefly, and then read the final question with precise pronunciation. Do not emphasize any possible answer clue."><s>Why will the woman stay home this afternoon?</s></mstts:express-as></voice></speak>
